    <string name="difficulty_guide_button_description">Explain difficulty levels</string>
    <string name="difficulty_guide_title">Difficulty guide</string>
    <string name="difficulty_guide_message"><b>Level 1 - Beginner</b>\nLast Digit and obvious Naked Singles.\n\n<b>Level 2 - Beginner</b>\nNaked Singles with fewer clues or a longer, less obvious solve path.\n\n<b>Level 3 - Easy</b>\nA small number of Hidden Singles.\n\n<b>Level 4 - Easy</b>\nHeavier Hidden-Single work, Pointing Candidates, and Claiming Candidates.\n\n<b>Level 5 - Moderate</b>\nNaked Pairs and Hidden Pairs. Repeated locked candidates can also reach this level.\n\n<b>Level 6 - Moderate</b>\nNaked or Hidden Triples and Quads, or sustained pair and locked-candidate work.\n\n<b>Level 7 - Hard</b>\nX-Wing, Skyscraper, and 2-String Kite.\n\n<b>Level 8 - Hard</b>\nSwordfish, XY-Wing, XYZ-Wing, W-Wing, and Simple Coloring. Several Level-7 deductions can also reach this level.\n\n<b>Level 9 - Challenge</b>\nJellyfish, X-Chain, and XY-Chain.\n\n<b>Level 10 - Challenge</b>\nForcing Chains or a forcing proof after the supported logical techniques are exhausted.</string>

